{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws","id":1061751,"title":"Lex Magica Gold Laws","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-13T00:37:28-07:00","id":1061751,"title":"Lex Magica Gold Laws","content":"In my archeomancy \u2018London\u2019 game I have Silver Ladder Lictor PC that want\u2019s to find new Gold Laws in Temples of Time Before. Problem is I do not know how to make them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> As 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook gives us this definition:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 2E, p.69</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Gold Laws</b> are those the Diamond believes were laws in the Time Before, gathered from Artifacts, from time-lost ruins, and by the agreement of multiple Consilia. Gold Laws are rare, and mostly concern the individual rights of mages to follow their studies unless they conflict with another\u2019s, to maintain sancta and Hallows without fear of trespass, and to be recognized for greater skill in the Arcana.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, clearly, Great Rights from <b>Sanctum &amp; Sigil</b> ( p. 26 ) are one of the Gold Laws. To remind those:<ul><li><b>Right of Crossing:</b> Let no borders stop an Awakened with a clear heart.</li> <li><b>Right of Emeritus:</b> Those who have earned respect must be treated with respect.</li> <li><b>Right of Hospitality:</b> Those who request hospitality must be granted it.</li> <li><b>Right of Nemesis:</b> When vengeance is declared, let none stand in its way.</li> <li><b>Right of Sanctuary:</b> Protect your home, and let no action cause it harm.</li> </ul>Any I think new does not seems \u2018universal\u2019 enough to those. Maybe someone have other examples of Gold Laws? Or idea what, exactly, could they concern?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-13-2017, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T01:12:24-07:00","id":1061755,"title":"","content":"You can't find a &quot;Golden Law&quot;. You can find a potential material and source for a Golden Law. Just because you found Atlantean Tablet that orders every Mage to wear a funny hat every Sunday or else they will be considered enemies of the Atlantis doesn't mean that multiple modern Consilia will agree to acknowledge it as a Gold Law. It won't be automatically respected and considerd THE law. However, you probably will have an interesting political whiff and whoffing, because some people will legit think you should make it THE LAW, while others will lobby for it just to spite the current rulers and paint them as evil anti antlantheans. <br /> <br /> So I suggest something that would impact daily lives of mages and challenge something they find very common and accepted; something like outlawing popular spell casting option [&quot;Self is Perfection, and sustaining self targeting spells is spitting in the eye of perfection, thus anyone who cast self buffs is unperfect, and thus suspicious and criminal by default&quot;; &quot;Human Sacrifice is only reasonable and allowable Sacrament Yantra&quot;; &quot;Love is an illusion that leads to downfall, any mage feeling funny in the tummy should Mana Purge the feeling or be considered dangerous to the society&quot;]. Imagine stumbling upon an ancient manifesto written by a extreme ideological group...but because it's ancient, you actually lack context to know it's just a manifesto, so you think that they all really wore these funny hats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T01:13:53-07:00","id":1061756,"title":"","content":"You know the character doesn't actually have to succeed right? Stories can also be about failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T01:16:46-07:00","id":1061757,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I would suggest a story that showcases process of declaring something found in a Temple Gold Law, emphasizing political and social discourse it invites and other ideological mayhem. Maybe a month or two where consilium tests that new thing...and, after everything is said and done, lessons learned, points made, they all go &quot;yeah, let's not go there&quot;, your player included.<br /> <br /> Kind of like Chinese say &quot;Democracy seems great for democratic countries, but it's unsuited for our society and would be a great mayhem&quot;, &quot;Atlantean laws seem great for Atlantis, but aren't necessarily The Best Idea for the world we live in&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T01:58:19-07:00","id":1061763,"title":"","content":"Well, to have story at all I <i>need</i> the Law that Convocations can decide if should be Gold in the first place. And as I understand correctly, to be Gold Law, this rule should be need to be found in <i>few</i> Temples first, like two or three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T04:04:38-07:00","id":1061778,"title":"","content":"Figure out the meta-purpose behind the Law first, then design one to fill it. What role do you want it to fill in your Chronicle? Because it's such a massive theme that could easily be a central thing of a given game for months, or it could be literally a one shot tv episode that everyone will forget next week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T05:41:34-07:00","id":1061794,"title":"","content":"It should be few session character arc. Best would related somehow to Hieromagus, rising Time Before civilizations or Earths Chakras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T08:18:06-07:00","id":1061827,"title":"","content":"I, for one, feel that Consiliums these days have too few hats and welcome the revealed Wisdom of our Atlantean forebears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T08:49:07-07:00","id":1061844,"title":"","content":"Do you want it to be a potential major change in the setting, or to the contrary, something small? &quot;Status Quo has to be maintained&quot; versus &quot;I don't mind if something big like USA becoming Magocracy happens&quot; offers different angles to approach this conundrum from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T10:30:05-07:00","id":1061874,"title":"","content":"You could probably have a long arc out of a Golden Rule(s) around the Right of the Master/Right of the Apprentice and its role in each aspect of society. If enough evidence existed that master/student relationship had preference over mage/order, then a recognized Golden Rule would stir up issues of loyalty with cross trained mages. Prolific teachers might end up with more political power due to apprentice obligations. What if a Golden Rule declares an apprentice's apprentice also owed loyalty/duty back to his master's master, ect. The possible specifics are endless.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs far as I know, right now, most of these issues are generalized by Order and then interpreted by individuals, but the possibility of a new Golden Rule and the political back in forth about it could be a huge monkey wrench in established mage society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3385-ckobbe","name":"ckobbe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T10:48:01-07:00","id":1061880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws#post1061751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe someone have other examples of Gold Laws?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the Great Rights and the right to duel, the Silver Ladder book has two examples:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Exchequer of Immanent Verbs is forbidden from authorizing trade with the Topaz-Eyed Mummery, </div> </div> </div>and the institution of the Guardian Interfector.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T11:47:46-07:00","id":1061894,"title":"","content":"'The Exchequer of Immanent Verbs is forbidden from authorizing trade with the Topaz-Eyed Mummery,' - WHAT does that even mean?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T11:53:39-07:00","id":1061897,"title":"","content":"It means there are plenty of &quot;gold&quot; laws that don't make any sense in the modern context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T12:01:51-07:00","id":1061902,"title":"","content":"The Gold Law is a bit like the Talmud. It's important but not necessarily relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T14:58:03-07:00","id":1062006,"title":"","content":"Said Rabbi Eliezer to them, &quot;If the Halakah is according to me, may the river run backwards!&quot; And so, the waters turned back and flowed up the hill.<br /> <br /> &quot;One cannot prove anything from a river,&quot; the Rabbis said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T19:06:19-07:00","id":1062129,"title":"","content":"From what I understand text of <b>Silver Ladder</b> Orderbook on matter, Gold Laws are showing in at least few Time Before sites and by this they are validate as 'Supernal in origin'. So theoretically it could simply be Law of 'Wore fancy hats' in 3 Atlantean sites and all that is needed to make a case with Lex Magica?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T19:11:06-07:00","id":1062131,"title":"","content":"Nuh-uh. Gold Laws are laws that independently arose in at least three geographically isolated Consilia; the idea being that, if groups of totally disparate Mages all simultaneously thought up this idea, it <i>must</i> be Supernally-inspired.<br /> <br /> (In 1e, it was tied to a belief that it must be some relic of the Atlantean diaspora, but since the diaspora never happened...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T19:25:19-07:00","id":1062132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1062131#post1062131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nuh-uh. Gold Laws are laws that independently arose in at least three geographically isolated Consilia; the idea being that, if groups of totally disparate Mages all simultaneously thought up this idea, it <i>must</i> be Supernally-inspired.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is interesting problem in my particular chronicle - We have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/101831-earth-s-chakras-and-awakened\">Earth's Chakras Temples</a> my PCs are 'visiting' ( more accurate would be 'robbing' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) . Sites were risen by group of Time Before Archmasters, each by his own device. ( Well, more like <i>To the Strongest</i> Archmasters that <b>pose</b> as to be truly from Time Before. Maybe more like 15-12 century BCE they are... ) If there would be common Law in at least 3 sites of them, would it still be 'Supernal' enough? /Taking in account that lower mages all <i>assume</i> Archmasters are really from Time Before./<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1062131#post1062131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(In 1e, it was tied to a belief that it must be some relic of the Atlantean diaspora, but since the diaspora never happened...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't let it fool you! Disapora was, only it was reality edited by Exarchs! We have evidance - for one, Darshanas... &lt; Start all the 'Atlantean' rambling on last Silver Ladder meeting &gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T11:30:02-07:00","id":1062389,"title":"","content":"&quot;Every member of the state must tithe their quintessential power to the Great Work.&quot;<br /> &quot;Every Grimoire must be presented to the Visus for review and catalog.&quot;<br /> &quot;The innocent have nothing to hide from the Veil.&quot;<br /> &quot;In honor of the pact with her Illumined Hand, the City of the Enlightened shall never again combine the runes of majesty and darkness.&quot;<br /> <br /> No one says that the laws have to be <i>real</i> or remotely a good idea. Or, as mentioned, comprehensible.<br /> The sites can be forgeries, too, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:00:45-07:00","id":1062414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1062389#post1062389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Every Grimoire must be presented to the Visus for review and catalog.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Visus Draconis as part of Gold Law is too much in 2E - if Diamond Orders are creation of Roman Republic ( or at least dates seems to point this in corebook and Dark Eras ) you cannot have Visus Draconis as Order mentioned in Time Before sites - as it is was <i>not created</i>, yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-14T12:29:39-07:00","id":1062433,"title":"","content":"Who said it's Visus Draconis. It's just &quot;Visus&quot;. It could be a specific Mage, a function, a stone face in the middle of a lake...<br /> I really like idea of a mysterious sentence or two, or an &quot;order&quot; that isn't very clear. Make it reappear three or four times in different temples, and instead of focusing your efforts on &quot;how to make the Law clear&quot;, create something that could be INTERPRETED differently by a lot of interested parties. OF COURSE Visus is Visus Draconis. OF COURSE Visus is not Visus Draconis, but a specific function, and we totally have a valid candidate for that. Etc.<br /> <br /> Basically, use the potential Law as a catalyst to emphasize how different parties want to push their agendas and what is their idea of better society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T02:36:19-07:00","id":1069939,"title":"","content":"I just got possible idea/question - What if Archmasters would be trolling Silver Ladder? <b>If their Chantires are Temples of Time Before, Archmasters just need to point 'Chosen One (Hieromagus) should rule the humans' as Law inscribed in their Temple and Silver Ladder should follow it, does it not?</b> Connected topic to this - How to extract possible Golden Law from the Temple that is in deep Astral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:20:52-07:00","id":1069951,"title":"","content":"The SL doesn't believe in the Heiragus and chantries don't count as ruins of the Time Before. The Guardians wouldn't take it at face value either, All Thrones Are False dictates they would test any potential Heiromagus harshly, including assasination attempts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T03:45:12-07:00","id":1069953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1069951#post1069951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SL doesn't believe in the Heiragus</div> </div> </div> </div>They do not need to - 'Golden Law' says they need to. Also, SL believs in Atlantean Royality, Blood of Dragon - easily our 'Troll Law' can point to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1069951#post1069951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">chantries don't count as ruins of the Time Before.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we have PreFall Archmasters, it's moot point. For me 'PreFall Secret Realm of Magic' works as Temple of Time Before by ( loose ) definition, whatever in Archmasters souls or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1069951#post1069951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guardians wouldn't take it at face value either, All Thrones Are False dictates they would test any potential Heiromagus harshly, including assasination attempts.</div> </div> </div> </div>We do <i>not</i> talk here about Guardians - it's entirely other thing and other discussion. We talk here about Golden Laws and their uncovering for Silver Ladders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T04:08:13-07:00","id":1069960,"title":"","content":"If the SL happened to find a reference to the Heiragus in a ruin from the Time Before they might look into it, but they still wouldn't accept it on blind faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T04:47:44-07:00","id":1069973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1069951#post1069951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">chantries don't count as ruins of the Time Before.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Wyrd's point is that a normal mage potentially wouldn't know the difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>If their Chantires are Temples of Time Before, Archmasters just need to point 'Chosen One (Hieromagus) should rule the humans' as Law inscribed in their Temple and Silver Ladder should follow it, does it not?</b> </div> </div> </div>It's a reasonable idea I think. Presumably lots of them are going to question it, but yeah I could see it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T05:12:20-07:00","id":1069987,"title":"","content":"The Orders don't blindly follow the Gold Laws<br /> <br /> Or anything for that matter, generally. Mages are sterner stuff than most.<br /> <br /> If a new Gold Law was found demanding some pretty heinous shit I very much doubt the Silver Ladder would just buy in. Or anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":117,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","user":"Solar","date":". 03-29-2017, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:19:13-07:00","id":1070085,"title":"","content":"What evidence of Golden Law Silver Ladder would need? Like image, writing, being possible to go to Temple of Time Before of any member?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T08:23:37-07:00","id":1070092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1070085#post1070085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What evidence of Golden Law Silver Ladder would need? Like image, writing, being possible to go to Temple of Time Before of any member?</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd need to be able to bring back an artifact or for others to go to the site and for either of those to be under the temporal inscrutability that the stuff from the Time Before has as a defining characteristic at the very least.<br /> <br /> That's to say nothing of the verification and process which would probably require at least a Convocation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:45:24-07:00","id":1070632,"title":"","content":"And probably find the same law recorded in different places before it is even taken into consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:05:01-07:00","id":1070643,"title":"","content":"Yeah, one of the reasons the current gold laws are set is because they've been found all kinds of places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T21:54:21-07:00","id":1071040,"title":"","content":"But how to get evidence from Astral Realms Temple? From Shadow Realm or Underworld one you just bring stuff with you. But in Astral one you do not have material component...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T22:25:45-07:00","id":1071062,"title":"","content":"Couple options for the ST:<br /> 1. You don't. No matter what, some are going to doubt it &amp; for good reason. <br /> 2. Let the players get creative.<br /> 3. Magic. There are ways to pull artifacts out of Astral Space. Some allow it to remain intact, too. You could let it be a known thing in certain circles that any artifact that can be embodied in the material world by using a specific set of spells and rituals and is an Artifact on completion comes from the Time Before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T04:37:21-07:00","id":1071182,"title":"","content":"Mind4+Matter 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:29:04-07:00","id":1071217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1071182#post1071182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind4+Matter 4</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That was in 1E. Now it should be enough to cast Goetic Summons which needs Mind 3 and Death/Spirit 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:36:39-07:00","id":1071220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1071217#post1071217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was in 1E. Now it should be enough to cast Goetic Summons which needs Mind 3 and Death/Spirit 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, the Matter would just make it material, no need for Death or Spirit though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:51:20-07:00","id":1071226,"title":"","content":"If it originates from the Astral then it should be ephemeral. Death and Spirit can be used to grant entities Manifestations (such as Materialize). I suppose they should be able to do that to other types of ephemeral matter too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T07:20:57-07:00","id":1071236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1071220#post1071220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, the Matter would just make it material, no need for Death or Spirit though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Some Mind - Matter Weaving will make it material but without Manifestation it will stay in Twilight. You can gran't it later but still, you have to.<br /> With Mind 4 Matter 4 you can just rip it from astral and don't bother with Twilights but it's not easily achievable to be a double Adept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-31-2017, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T07:48:40-07:00","id":1071248,"title":"","content":"Twilight is far enough into the Fallen to make it observable to anyone with Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T21:34:42-07:00","id":1071602,"title":"","content":"Thinking about example Law I want to mark my PCs as possible rulers of the Fallen World - at certin way of reading it. They are strongly marked as 'Nine' on their Destiny when seen by Fate mages. And now to the sentence I try to phrase:<br /> <br /> <i>'Nine will lead the World, so as the people in it'.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T03:05:56-07:00","id":1071665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1061751-lex-magica-gold-laws?p=1071602#post1071602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>'Nine will lead the World, so as the people in it'.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>That's sounds pretty good although I'm not sure what 'so as the people in it' means. I mean, it sounds like the kind of phrasing a prophecy would have, just I don't quite know what it's trying to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T03:45:32-07:00","id":1071671,"title":"","content":"I meant sentace point that 'Nine' will lead mages and Awakening should listen to him/them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}